That is a substantially better agentic story than “agent can buy a domain.” name.com already supports the basic Search → Register → Manage workflow. What we're adding is the **reasoning and empirical optimization layer that determines what should be bought**. Their current API gives us live purchasability, purchase price, renewal price, premium status and purchase type, so these constraints can be first-class inputs to the algorithm. ([name.com Core API][1])

And it maps extremely well to their hackathon criteria: deep API use, unexpected application, technical execution, real-world viability and an integration visible in the demo. ([DevNetwork Hackathon 2026][2])

