# 15. Don't create a fake master score

The UI should show:

```text
FACTMOLE.DEV

Semantic transmission      84%
Pairwise win probability   73%
Model stability            92%
Worst-family result        79%
Brand elasticity           71%
Agent task recognition     88%

NAME.COM
Purchasable                 YES
First year                  $14.99
Renewal                     $14.99
Premium                     NO
```

Then:

> **Recommended under your constraints**

rather than:

> AI DOMAIN SCORE = 94.382

Internally, though, the optimizer needs a policy.

Use **Pareto dominance first**.

Candidate A dominates B if it is no worse on every selected objective and strictly better on at least one.

Only when multiple Pareto-optimal candidates remain should a policy choose.

For example:

[
U =
w_sS+
w_pP+
w_mM+
w_eE+
w_aA+
w_cC
]

where weights are determined by the user's requested objective.

For:

> developer API optimized for agents

use greater weight on semantic transmission, agent recognition and model stability.

For:

> consumer lifestyle brand

increase memorability and elasticity.

Explicitly label these policy weights as **decision policy**, not scientific truth.

