# 33. Why this could become genuinely valuable to name.com

The long-term API isn't really:

```text
search domains
```

It's:

```text
recommend the best purchasable domain
for this product under these constraints
```

And behind that endpoint sits:

```text
name.com inventory
+
naming experiments
+
model-family behavior
+
actual registration decisions
+
eventual downstream performance
```

Every time someone selects and registers a domain, DomainArena gets a stronger revealed-preference signal.

Eventually:

[
P(\text{registration}\mid
name,\ price,\ TLD,\ intent,\ audience)
]

and later:

[
P(\text{successful adoption}\mid
name,\ TLD,\ intent,\ audience)
]

become learnable.

That is why the system could drive demand **into name.com's API instead of competing with name.com**.

They provide the market and transaction infrastructure.

DomainArena provides the decision intelligence.

That is the relationship I would make central in the sponsor pitch.

